{
  "passages": [
    {
      "id": "m51",
      "about_topic": true,
      "says": "fact: motorcycles, bicycles, limited-speed motorcycles and mopeds often pull to the side of the lane; rule: do not pass in the same lane; rule: pass these vehicles by changing lanes"
    },
    {
      "id": "m1",
      "about_topic": true,
      "says": "fact: changing position on the road involves changing lanes or overtaking and passing another vehicle"
    },
    {
      "id": "m4",
      "about_topic": true,
      "says": "rule: be sure there is enough space and time to complete the move safely before beginning a change of position"
    },
    {
      "id": "m2",
      "about_topic": true,
      "says": "definition: passing is changing lanes to move past a slower vehicle"
    },
    {
      "id": "m3",
      "about_topic": true,
      "says": "fact: not all vehicles travel at the same speed; cyclists, road service vehicles and drivers preparing to turn are usually slower than through traffic"
    },
    {
      "id": "m5",
      "about_topic": true,
      "says": "rule: never overtake and pass unless sure it can be done without danger to self or others"
    },
    {
      "id": "m72",
      "about_topic": true,
      "says": "rule: do not pass moving snow plows under any conditions"
    },
    {
      "id": "m6",
      "about_topic": true,
      "says": "rule: if in doubt, do not pass"
    },
    {
      "id": "m8",
      "about_topic": true,
      "says": "lead: introduces the steps for passing a vehicle"
    },
    {
      "id": "m9",
      "about_topic": true,
      "says": "procedure step: use left-turn signal and check that the way is clear ahead and before moving into the passing lane"
    },
    {
      "id": "m10",
      "about_topic": true,
      "says": "procedure step: watch for hidden bicycles and small vehicles, vehicles turning left, and vehicles or pedestrians entering the road"
    },
    {
      "id": "m11",
      "about_topic": true,
      "says": "procedure step: change lanes only after signalling; after overtaking, signal to move back and change lanes when the entire front is visible in the inside mirror"
    },
    {
      "id": "m12",
      "about_topic": true,
      "says": "rule: be careful not to cut off a vehicle by suddenly moving in front of it"
    },
    {
      "id": "m13",
      "about_topic": true,
      "says": "rule: if the vehicle being passed speeds up, do not race; go back to the original lane"
    },
    {
      "id": "m85",
      "about_topic": true,
      "says": "rule (law): do not speed up when another driver is trying to pass; it is unlawful and dangerous"
    },
    {
      "id": "m14",
      "about_topic": true,
      "says": "figure: diagram showing how to pass another vehicle"
    },
    {
      "id": "m15",
      "about_topic": true,
      "says": "rule (law): passing within 30 m of a pedestrian crossover is not permitted"
    },
    {
      "id": "m17",
      "about_topic": true,
      "says": "rule (law): passing left of a centreline is not permitted within 30 m of a bridge, viaduct or tunnel"
    },
    {
      "id": "m18",
      "about_topic": true,
      "says": "rule: do not pass when approaching the crest of a hill or on a curve with obstructed vision and insufficient clear distance"
    },
    {
      "id": "m50",
      "about_topic": true,
      "says": "rule: when passing parked vehicles, watch for people suddenly opening doors or doors opened to load and unload"
    },
    {
      "id": "m84",
      "about_topic": true,
      "says": "rule: when faster traffic wants to pass, move to the right and let it pass in safety"
    },
    {
      "id": "m89",
      "about_topic": true,
      "says": "rule: when being passed on an undivided road, pay attention to oncoming traffic and move closer to the right side; be prepared to slow down to prevent a collision"
    },
    {
      "id": "m90",
      "about_topic": true,
      "says": "fact: on many 3+ lane high-speed roads trucks are not allowed in the far left lane, making the next lane the truck passing lane; rule: move right when a truck wants to pass"
    },
    {
      "id": "m52",
      "about_topic": true,
      "says": "figure: diagram showing how to pass another vehicle at night"
    },
    {
      "id": "m39",
      "about_topic": true,
      "says": "rule: be very careful when passing at night"
    },
    {
      "id": "m40",
      "about_topic": true,
      "says": "lead: introduces steps for passing at night when the way is clear"
    },
    {
      "id": "m41",
      "about_topic": true,
      "says": "procedure step: switch headlights to low beams as you approach from behind"
    },
    {
      "id": "m42",
      "about_topic": true,
      "says": "procedure step: signal, check mirrors and blind spot, pull out to pass; switch on high beams alongside the vehicle"
    },
    {
      "id": "m43",
      "about_topic": true,
      "says": "procedure step: when the front of the vehicle is visible in the rear view mirror, pull back into the right lane and signal"
    },
    {
      "id": "m27",
      "about_topic": true,
      "says": "figure: diagram of a passing or climbing lane"
    },
    {
      "id": "m28",
      "about_topic": true,
      "says": "fact: some roads have special passing or climbing lanes that let slower vehicles move right so faster ones can pass in the left lane"
    },
    {
      "id": "m29",
      "about_topic": true,
      "says": "fact: an advance sign warns of an upcoming passing lane; another sign warns when the lane is ending so drivers can merge"
    },
    {
      "id": "m38",
      "about_topic": true,
      "says": "rule (law): may drive on the right shoulder only to pass a left-turning vehicle and only if paved; rule (law): may not pass on the left shoulder, paved or not"
    },
    {
      "id": "m35",
      "about_topic": true,
      "says": "fact: most passing is done on the left; rule (law): may pass on the right on multi-lane or one-way roads and when overtaking a streetcar or a left-turning vehicle"
    },
    {
      "id": "m36",
      "about_topic": true,
      "says": "fact: passing on the right can be more dangerous than passing on the left"
    },
    {
      "id": "m37",
      "about_topic": true,
      "says": "rule: if in the left most lane with a slower vehicle ahead, wait for it to move right; rule: do not suddenly change lanes and pass on the right"
    },
    {
      "id": "m61",
      "about_topic": true,
      "says": "figure: vehicle stopped the required 2 m behind the rear doors of a stopped streetcar"
    },
    {
      "id": "m62",
      "about_topic": true,
      "says": "rule (law): must pass streetcars on the right unless on a one-way road"
    },
    {
      "id": "m63",
      "about_topic": true,
      "says": "rule (law): stay at least 2 m behind the rear doors at streetcar stops where passengers get on/off; does not apply where an area is set aside for streetcar passengers"
    },
    {
      "id": "m64",
      "about_topic": true,
      "says": "rule: always pass streetcar stop areas at a reasonable speed and be prepared for pedestrians to make sudden or unexpected moves"
    }
  ],
  "statements": [
    {
      "id": "s1",
      "type": "DEFINE",
      "force": null,
      "force_from": null,
      "text": "DEFINE passing IS changing lanes to move past a slower vehicle",
      "sources": [
        {
          "id": "m2",
          "quote": "Passing is changing lanes to move past a slower vehicle."
        }
      ],
      "flags": [],
      "links": [],
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "s2",
      "type": "FACT",
      "force": null,
      "force_from": null,
      "text": "FACT changing position on the road involves changing lanes or overtaking and passing another vehicle",
      "sources": [
        {
          "id": "m1",
          "quote": "Changing your position on the road involves changing lanes or overtaking and passing another vehicle."
        }
      ],
      "flags": [],
      "links": [],
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "s3",
      "type": "FACT",
      "force": null,
      "force_from": null,
      "text": "FACT not all vehicles travel at the same speed; cyclists, road service vehicles and drivers preparing to turn are [?usually] slower than through traffic",
      "sources": [
        {
          "id": "m3",
          "quote": "While all public roads have speed limits, not all vehicles travel at the same speed. For example, cyclists, road service vehicles and drivers ahead that are preparing to turn are usually slower than the through traffic."
        }
      ],
      "flags": [
        {
          "code": "S",
          "span": "usually",
          "note": "Not all such vehicles are slower; the handbook hedges with 'usually'."
        }
      ],
      "links": [],
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "s4",
      "type": "RULE",
      "force": "ADVISORY",
      "force_from": "imperative (\"be sure\")",
      "text": "a driver SHOULD be sure there is [?enough] space and time to complete the move [?safely] WHEN the driver is about to change position on the road",
      "sources": [
        {
          "id": "m4",
          "quote": "Before beginning, be sure you have enough space and time to complete the move safely."
        },
        {
          "id": "m1",
          "quote": "Changing your position on the road involves changing lanes or overtaking and passing another vehicle."
        }
      ],
      "flags": [
        {
          "code": "J",
          "span": "enough",
          "note": "No measure of space or time is given."
        },
        {
          "code": "J",
          "span": "safely",
          "note": "No objective test for safe completion of the move."
        }
      ],
      "links": [],
      "note": "The rule applies to all changes of position, including passing, as established by m1."
    },
    {
      "id": "s5",
      "type": "RULE",
      "force": "ADVISORY",
      "force_from": "imperative (\"Never\")",
      "text": "a driver SHOULD NOT overtake and pass another vehicle UNLESS the driver is [?sure] the driver can do so without [?danger] to the driver or others",
      "sources": [
        {
          "id": "m5",
          "quote": "Never overtake and pass another vehicle unless you are sure you can do so without danger to yourself or others."
        }
      ],
      "flags": [
        {
          "code": "J",
          "span": "sure",
          "note": "Subjective certainty; no observable test."
        },
        {
          "code": "J",
          "span": "danger",
          "note": "No objective measure of what constitutes danger."
        }
      ],
      "links": [],
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "s6",
      "type": "RULE",
      "force": "ADVISORY",
      "force_from": "imperative (\"do not pass\")",
      "text": "a driver SHOULD NOT pass WHEN [?in doubt]",
      "sources": [
        {
          "id": "m6",
          "quote": "If in doubt, do not pass."
        }
      ],
      "flags": [
        {
          "code": "J",
          "span": "in doubt",
          "note": "No objective test for when a driver is in doubt."
        }
      ],
      "links": [],
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "s7",
      "type": "RULE",
      "force": "ADVISORY",
      "force_from": "imperative (\"Don't pass\")",
      "text": "a driver SHOULD NOT pass a moving snow plow under any conditions",
      "sources": [
        {
          "id": "m72",
          "quote": "Don't pass moving snow plows under any conditions."
        }
      ],
      "flags": [],
      "links": [],
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "s8",
      "type": "RULE",
      "force": "LEGAL",
      "force_from": "text (\"It is unlawful\")",
      "text": "a driver MUST NOT speed up WHEN another driver is trying to pass the driver BECAUSE it is dangerous",
      "sources": [
        {
          "id": "m85",
          "quote": "And do not speed up when another driver is trying to pass you. It is unlawful and dangerous."
        }
      ],
      "flags": [],
      "links": [],
      "note": "\"It is unlawful\" gives legal force to the prohibition."
    },
    {
      "id": "s9",
      "type": "RULE",
      "force": "LEGAL",
      "force_from": "text (\"is not permitted\")",
      "text": "a driver MUST NOT pass within 30 m of a pedestrian crossover",
      "sources": [
        {
          "id": "m15",
          "quote": "Passing within 30 metres of a pedestrian crossover is not permitted."
        }
      ],
      "flags": [],
      "links": [],
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "s10",
      "type": "RULE",
      "force": "LEGAL",
      "force_from": "text (\"is not permitted\")",
      "text": "a driver MUST NOT pass to the left of a centreline within 30 m of a bridge, viaduct or tunnel",
      "sources": [
        {
          "id": "m17",
          "quote": "Passing left of a centreline is not permitted 30 metres from a bridge, viaduct or tunnel."
        }
      ],
      "flags": [],
      "links": [],
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "s11",
      "type": "RULE",
      "force": "ADVISORY",
      "force_from": "imperative (\"Don't attempt\")",
      "text": "a driver SHOULD NOT attempt to pass WHEN approaching the crest of a hill OR on a curve AND the driver's vision of oncoming traffic is obstructed AND there is not [?enough] clear distance ahead to pass in [?safety]",
      "sources": [
        {
          "id": "m18",
          "quote": "Don't attempt to pass when approaching the crest of a hill or on a curve where your vision of oncoming traffic is obstructed and there is not enough clear distance ahead to pass in safety."
        }
      ],
      "flags": [
        {
          "code": "J",
          "span": "enough",
          "note": "No measure of clear distance is given."
        },
        {
          "code": "J",
          "span": "safety",
          "note": "No objective test for passing in safety."
        }
      ],
      "links": [],
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "s12",
      "type": "RULE",
      "force": "ADVISORY",
      "force_from": "caution (\"watch carefully\")",
      "text": "a driver SHOULD WATCH FOR people suddenly opening doors or doors opened to load and unload WHEN passing parked vehicles",
      "sources": [
        {
          "id": "m50",
          "quote": "When passing parked vehicles, watch carefully for people suddenly opening doors or for doors opened to load and unload."
        }
      ],
      "flags": [],
      "links": [],
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "s13",
      "type": "FACT",
      "force": null,
      "force_from": null,
      "text": "FACT motorcycles, bicycles, limited-speed motorcycles and mopeds [?often] need to pull to the left or right side of their lane to avoid dangerous road conditions or to be seen by other drivers",
      "sources": [
        {
          "id": "m51",
          "quote": "Motorcycles, bicycles, limited-speed motorcycles and mopeds often need to pull to the left or right side of their lane to avoid dangerous road conditions or to be seen by other drivers."
        }
      ],
      "flags": [
        {
          "code": "S",
          "span": "often",
          "note": "Not always; the frequency is hedged."
        }
      ],
      "links": [],
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "s14",
      "type": "RULE",
      "force": "ADVISORY",
      "force_from": "imperative (\"Do not take\")",
      "text": "a driver SHOULD NOT pass a motorcycle, bicycle, limited-speed motorcycle or moped in the same lane WHEN the vehicle pulls to the side of the lane",
      "sources": [
        {
          "id": "m51",
          "quote": "Do not take this as an invitation to pass in the same lane."
        }
      ],
      "flags": [],
      "links": [],
      "note": "\"This\" refers to the vehicle pulling to the side of the lane, as described in the preceding sentence."
    },
    {
      "id": "s15",
      "type": "RULE",
      "force": "ADVISORY",
      "force_from": "imperative (\"do so by changing lanes\")",
      "text": "a driver SHOULD pass a motorcycle, bicycle, limited-speed motorcycle or moped by changing lanes WHEN the driver wants to pass the vehicle",
      "sources": [
        {
          "id": "m51",
          "quote": "If you do want to pass these vehicles, do so by changing lanes."
        }
      ],
      "flags": [],
      "links": [],
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "s16",
      "type": "PROCEDURE",
      "force": "ADVISORY",
      "force_from": "imperative steps",
      "text": "TO pass a vehicle",
      "steps": [
        {
          "n": "1",
          "text": "use the left-turn signal to show that the driver wants to pass AND check that the way is clear ahead and behind",
          "sources": [
            "m9"
          ]
        },
        {
          "n": "2",
          "text": "watch for bicycles and small vehicles that may be hidden from view in front of the vehicle, vehicles that may be turning left, and vehicles or pedestrians entering the road from another road or driveway",
          "sources": [
            "m10"
          ]
        },
        {
          "n": "3",
          "text": "change lanes into the passing lane only after signalling",
          "sources": [
            "m11"
          ]
        },
        {
          "n": "4",
          "text": "after overtaking, signal that the driver wants to move back into the starting lane",
          "sources": [
            "m11"
          ]
        },
        {
          "n": "5",
          "text": "when the driver can see the entire front of the vehicle in the inside mirror, make the lane change back",
          "sources": [
            "m11"
          ]
        },
        {
          "n": "6",
          "text": "do not cut off a vehicle by suddenly moving in front of it",
          "sources": [
            "m12"
          ]
        },
        {
          "n": "IF",
          "text": "IF the vehicle being passed speeds up THEN do not race AND go back to the original lane",
          "sources": [
            "m13"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "sources": [
        {
          "id": "m8",
          "quote": "Here are the steps for passing a vehicle:"
        },
        {
          "id": "m14",
          "quote": "how to pass another vehicle"
        }
      ],
      "flags": [],
      "links": [
        "s17",
        "s18"
      ],
      "note": "Steps 6 and the IF branch are also standalone rules (s17, s18)."
    },
    {
      "id": "s17",
      "type": "RULE",
      "force": "ADVISORY",
      "force_from": "caution (\"Be careful not to\")",
      "text": "a driver SHOULD NOT cut off a vehicle by suddenly moving in front of it WHEN passing",
      "sources": [
        {
          "id": "m12",
          "quote": "Be careful not to cut off a vehicle by suddenly moving in front of it."
        }
      ],
      "flags": [],
      "links": [
        "s16"
      ],
      "note": "Also step 6 of the passing procedure."
    },
    {
      "id": "s18",
      "type": "RULE",
      "force": "ADVISORY",
      "force_from": "imperative (\"do not race\", \"Go back\")",
      "text": "a driver SHOULD NOT race AND SHOULD go back to the original lane WHEN the vehicle being passed speeds up",
      "sources": [
        {
          "id": "m13",
          "quote": "If the vehicle you are passing speeds up, do not race. Go back to your original lane."
        }
      ],
      "flags": [],
      "links": [
        "s16"
      ],
      "note": "Also the IF branch of the passing procedure."
    },
    {
      "id": "s19",
      "type": "RULE",
      "force": "ADVISORY",
      "force_from": "imperative (\"move\", \"let\")",
      "text": "a driver SHOULD move to the right AND let faster traffic pass in [?safety] WHEN faster traffic wants to pass the driver",
      "sources": [
        {
          "id": "m84",
          "quote": "When faster traffic wants to pass you, move to the right and let it pass in safety."
        }
      ],
      "flags": [
        {
          "code": "J",
          "span": "safety",
          "note": "No objective test for passing in safety."
        }
      ],
      "links": [],
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "s20",
      "type": "RULE",
      "force": "ADVISORY",
      "force_from": "imperative (\"pay attention\", \"move\")",
      "text": "a driver SHOULD pay attention to oncoming traffic AND move closer to the right side of the lane WHEN being passed on an undivided road AND the passing driver has pulled into the opposite lane",
      "sources": [
        {
          "id": "m89",
          "quote": "When being passed on an undivided road where the passing driver has pulled into the opposite lane, pay attention to oncoming traffic and move closer to the right side of the lane."
        }
      ],
      "flags": [],
      "links": [],
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "s21",
      "type": "RULE",
      "force": "ADVISORY",
      "force_from": "caution (\"Be prepared\")",
      "text": "a driver SHOULD be prepared to slow down WHEN being passed on an undivided road AND the passing driver has pulled into the opposite lane BECAUSE it lets the passing driver get in front more quickly to prevent a collision",
      "sources": [
        {
          "id": "m89",
          "quote": "Be prepared to slow down to let the passing driver get in front of you more quickly to prevent a collision."
        }
      ],
      "flags": [],
      "links": [],
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "s22",
      "type": "FACT",
      "force": null,
      "force_from": null,
      "text": "FACT on [?many] high-speed roads with 3 or more lanes in each direction, trucks are not allowed to drive in the far left-hand lane, and the lane next to it is the truck passing lane",
      "sources": [
        {
          "id": "m90",
          "quote": "On many high-speed roads with three or more lanes in each direction, trucks are not allowed to drive in the far left-hand lane. This means that the lane next to it is the truck passing lane."
        }
      ],
      "flags": [
        {
          "code": "S",
          "span": "many",
          "note": "Not all such roads; the scope is hedged."
        }
      ],
      "links": [],
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "s23",
      "type": "RULE",
      "force": "ADVISORY",
      "force_from": "imperative (\"move\")",
      "text": "a driver SHOULD move into the right-hand lane [?as soon as the driver can] WHEN in the truck passing lane on a high-speed road with 3 or more lanes in each direction AND a truck wants to pass the driver",
      "sources": [
        {
          "id": "m90",
          "quote": "If you are in this lane and a truck wants to pass, move into the right-hand lane as soon as you can."
        }
      ],
      "flags": [
        {
          "code": "J",
          "span": "as soon as the driver can",
          "note": "No measure of how quickly the lane change must be made."
        }
      ],
      "links": [
        "s22"
      ],
      "note": "\"This lane\" in the handbook refers to the truck passing lane defined in the preceding sentence."
    },
    {
      "id": "s24",
      "type": "RULE",
      "force": "ADVISORY",
      "force_from": "caution (\"Be very careful\")",
      "text": "a driver SHOULD be very careful WHEN passing at night",
      "sources": [
        {
          "id": "m39",
          "quote": "Be very careful when you pass other vehicles at night."
        }
      ],
      "flags": [],
      "links": [],
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "s25",
      "type": "PROCEDURE",
      "force": "ADVISORY",
      "force_from": "imperative steps",
      "text": "TO pass a vehicle at night WHEN the way is clear",
      "steps": [
        {
          "n": "1",
          "text": "switch the headlights to low beams as the driver approaches a vehicle from behind",
          "sources": [
            "m41"
          ]
        },
        {
          "n": "2",
          "text": "signal AND check the mirrors and blind spot AND pull out to pass",
          "sources": [
            "m42"
          ]
        },
        {
          "n": "3",
          "text": "switch on the high beams WHILE moving alongside the vehicle BECAUSE it lets the driver see more of the road ahead",
          "sources": [
            "m42"
          ]
        },
        {
          "n": "4",
          "text": "when the driver can see all of the front of the vehicle in the rear view mirror, pull back into the right lane AND signal",
          "sources": [
            "m43"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "sources": [
        {
          "id": "m40",
          "quote": "If you have to pass and the way is clear, follow these steps:"
        },
        {
          "id": "m52",
          "quote": "how to pass another vehicle"
        }
      ],
      "flags": [],
      "links": [],
      "note": "The at-night condition comes from the heading 'Passing at night'; the way-is-clear condition comes from m40."
    },
    {
      "id": "s26",
      "type": "FACT",
